WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.800
After a food-safety refresher, a shift supervisor asks each warehouse worker two or three questions,

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.720
then ticks one box on a form.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.210
The form does not capture which questions were asked,

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.540
what the worker said, or how the supervisor judged the answers;

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.980
the box records only that the conversation happened.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:25.790
We wanted to know whether that tick tells you what a worker still knows, three months on.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:30.630
So we went back to nine hundred workers across twenty-four warehouses,

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:34.850
and retested them in writing, on the same bank of questions.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.290
Workers with a ticked check averaged five point two out of eight;

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.533
workers without one, four point eight.

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.333
Not a meaningful difference:

00:00:42.633 --> 00:00:45.853
the two sets of scores sit almost on top of one another.

00:00:46.653 --> 00:00:50.263
In six warehouses, with everyone’s consent, we recorded the checks themselves.

00:00:50.563 --> 00:00:56.463
Where the box was ticked, ninety-eight point three per cent of recordings hold an exchange you can hear.

00:00:57.263 --> 00:01:00.746
So the tick is a reliable record that the check happened.

00:01:01.046 --> 00:01:03.229
But a worker whose check ran three minutes

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:07.449
scored, on average, no higher than one whose check ran ten seconds.

00:01:08.249 --> 00:01:11.349
The authors read the tick as accurate about procedure,

00:01:11.549 --> 00:01:13.267
and silent about substance.

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:16.287
They suggest reporting what workers still know alongside it.

00:01:17.087 --> 00:01:19.687
The box was never built to hold an answer.

00:01:19.987 --> 00:01:24.047
It was built to hold a supervisor’s word that a question got asked,

00:01:24.197 --> 00:01:28.877
and everyone reading it since has added a promise the form itself never made.
